From c23ff53f7378718602d2b3af35f98ecd639d7b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:03:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 390/393] gallium/pvr: keep client-filled textures uncompressed

A texture that the CPU fills before anything renders into it is a client
texture. TFBC saves DRAM bandwidth when such a texture is sampled, but on
this GPU sampling these textures compressed measured slower than
uncompressed (the cost is assumed to be in the texture unit; that was not
measured). With this condition behind a debug knob on series 0387 (before
0388 and 0389; two full runs each way), glmark2 bump (height) runs 6.7%
faster and jellyfish 6.5%, the whole run scores 838/839 -> 842/842, and no
scene drops by more than 0.31% (2.5 fps at most). Textures first written
by a GPU render keep TFBC.

At the first CPU write to a compressed texture that nothing has rendered
into, clear its fbc flag. The data address stays past the header area,
which is left unused; descriptors and PBE words are built from the flag at
use, so nothing holds the old state.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_context.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_context.c
index 54645949..9fa20275 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_context.c
@@ -50,6 +50,12 @@ pvr_transfer_map(struct pipe_context *pctx, struct pipe_resource *pres,
     * through a linear copy of the level: the GPU decodes it into the staging resource (unless the
     * content is discarded) and, after a write, encodes it back on unmap. Twiddled depth is only
     * written by the ZLS. */
+   /* A compressed level that nothing has rendered into and that the CPU writes first belongs to a
+    * client texture: keep it uncompressed (sampling such textures compressed measured slower).
+    * Textures first written by a GPU render keep TFBC. The data address stays past the unused
+    * header area, and descriptors and PBE words read the flag at use. */
+   if (res->fbc && res->write_seq == 0 && (usage & PIPE_MAP_WRITE))
+      res->fbc = false;
    if (res->twiddled) {
       struct pvr_context *ctx = pvr_context(pctx);
       /* A cube map is mapped one face at a time: the box's z selects the face. */
-- 
